{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>These are the heads of their fathers' houses.</b> Because HaShem wished to give the third Torah through a tribe that was tripled in many kinds of tripling, as mentioned in the Gemara (Shabbat 88a), He therefore began to investigate the heads of the fathers' houses. He found Reuben — four families; Simeon — five families; Levi — three families. He therefore disqualified the first ones and chose Levi, who was tripled twice. The commentators said that He first searched in Reuben, to see whether He would find among his sons a man after His own heart, fit for this mission — just as Samuel the prophet searched among the sons of Jesse. And we infer the searching from the searching there: just as there He disqualified the first ones until He found a man after His own heart, so too here He wished to search among the sons of Reuben and Simeon — and He searched and did not find, until He reached the stock of Levi and found Aaron and Moses, and then He no longer needed to search."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:29.239824349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}